          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dǎyìn is built from 打 'to strike' and yìn 'a seal', both inherited from Middle Chinese, taengX and 'jinH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second as a seal of office."
            }
